# Shell scripts must stay LF-terminated.
#
# core.autocrlf=true on Windows would otherwise check these out with CRLF, and
# bash then fails on the stray carriage returns -- in a shebang and in every
# line it tries to parse. tests/workflow/*.sh run under bash on the Linux
# runner, so a CRLF checkout breaks them only on the machine that could have
# caught it.
*.sh text eol=lf
